{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01153",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.7,
      "end_seconds": 5.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "Ready for you, doctor. I'll stay in case you need anything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 8.94,
      "end_seconds": 13.48,
      "duration_seconds": 4.54,
      "text": "Thanks. Hello, come in, sit down. What brings you in today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 14.39,
      "end_seconds": 21.4,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "Right, good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 23.26,
      "end_seconds": 36.29,
      "duration_seconds": 13.03,
      "text": "Yeah, it's shoulder tip pain. I don't know what's causing it. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.7,
      "end_seconds": 40.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.14,
      "text": "Which medicines do you take at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 42.36,
      "end_seconds": 51.15,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "It's a... um, you know, I can't remember what it's called. It's a small white one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 52.82,
      "end_seconds": 56.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Okay, do you remember what it's for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.06,
      "end_seconds": 74.69,
      "duration_seconds": 17.63,
      "text": "For the migraine prevention, I believe. My husband sets them out for me, I just take what I'm given. Well, you know, I had sumatriptan at one point, but I'm off it now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.09,
      "end_seconds": 93.35,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Can you tell me when it first started?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.36,
      "end_seconds": 100.78,
      "duration_seconds": 5.42,
      "text": "I mean, you know, around three days, I think."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 101.49,
      "end_seconds": 105.5,
      "duration_seconds": 4.01,
      "text": "Hm, I'd say more like five days."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 107.54,
      "end_seconds": 112.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.05,
      "text": "Okay, so roughly three to five days. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.58,
      "end_seconds": 116.64,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "That sounds about right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 117.74,
      "end_seconds": 126.41,
      "duration_seconds": 8.67,
      "text": "Can you describe it a bit more for me? How strong it is, what the pattern is, what helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 127.6,
      "end_seconds": 144.65,
      "duration_seconds": 17.05,
      "text": "So, you know, honestly, a couple of times a week. I'd say moderate. I told my wife I'd come today. I kept putting it off, which I know isn't sensible."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.46,
      "end_seconds": 152.41,
      "duration_seconds": 6.95,
      "text": "Okay, so I was just going to say that the main thing is—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 152.51,
      "end_seconds": 159.92,
      "duration_seconds": 7.41,
      "text": "Sorry to cut in, doctor, quick question: shall I bring the trolley in now or later?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 161.16,
      "end_seconds": 163.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.47,
      "text": "Later, thanks. Please go on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.55,
      "end_seconds": 177.77,
      "duration_seconds": 12.22,
      "text": "Oh, and light vaginal bleeding. Oh, um, and sharp pain low on one side. That's been about the same, two months."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.05,
      "end_seconds": 181.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.52,
      "text": "How often do you get it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 183.57,
      "end_seconds": 190.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "It's, um... not exactly... well, hard to explain, I mean—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.81,
      "end_seconds": 197.75,
      "duration_seconds": 5.94,
      "text": "Let me put it another way: how many times in a typical day or week?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 199.68,
      "end_seconds": 201.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "It's on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_5",
      "role": "UNKNOWN",
      "start_seconds": 203.78,
      "end_seconds": 206.09,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Yes, exactly like that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 207.73,
      "end_seconds": 211.3,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "So, did you notice any vaginal discharge?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 212.94,
      "end_seconds": 217.63,
      "duration_seconds": 4.69,
      "text": "Not at all, um, no vaginal discharge."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 219.33,
      "end_seconds": 220.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.17,
      "text": "How about fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.44,
      "end_seconds": 224.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.7,
      "text": "Nope, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 224.74,
      "end_seconds": 231.1,
      "duration_seconds": 6.36,
      "text": "Actually, uh, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 232.61,
      "end_seconds": 239.65,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 241.38,
      "end_seconds": 250.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.79,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Okay, anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 251.85,
      "end_seconds": 254.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.63,
      "text": "Nothing on the skin, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 255.57,
      "end_seconds": 258.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "What line of work are you in?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 262.09,
      "end_seconds": 267.26,
      "duration_seconds": 5.17,
      "text": "I'm a bus driver, so I sit for long hours."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 269.07,
      "end_seconds": 271.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Tell me about your eating."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 272.42,
      "end_seconds": 277.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.52,
      "text": "I drink a lot of tea and snack through the day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.5,
      "end_seconds": 282.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.84,
      "text": "Has anyone ever diagnosed you with something?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.18,
      "end_seconds": 292.66,
      "duration_seconds": 6.48,
      "text": "Uh, uh, I've had migraines for five years now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 310.5,
      "end_seconds": 313.89,
      "duration_seconds": 3.39,
      "text": "Did you ever have any procedures done?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 315.0,
      "end_seconds": 321.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.35,
      "text": "Yes, I had a caesarean for my second baby, nine years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 322.48,
      "end_seconds": 331.72,
      "duration_seconds": 9.24,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Temp 37.1 degrees, blood pressure 129 over 86, pulse is 117 beats a minute."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.44,
      "end_seconds": 354.53,
      "duration_seconds": 22.09,
      "text": "Thanks. From what you've told me, it points towards a possible ectopic pregnancy. I can't rule out a ruptured ovarian cyst yet. I'd like to arrange an urgent pelvic scan for possible ectopic. It's a routine test and it'll give us a much clearer picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 358.39,
      "end_seconds": 361.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.53,
      "text": "Where would I go for that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 363.59,
      "end_seconds": 385.04,
      "duration_seconds": 21.45,
      "text": "Let's get a pregnancy test, for pelvic pain and bleeding. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. You need to go to the hospital now for an emergency scan. The gynaecology team would be the right next step, I'll refer you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 385.92,
      "end_seconds": 386.62,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 388.64,
      "end_seconds": 396.64,
      "duration_seconds": 8.0,
      "text": "Please come and see me straight away. Right, that's the plan. Do you want to ask me anything?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 397.24,
      "end_seconds": 399.2,
      "duration_seconds": 1.96,
      "text": "That's clear, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.37,
      "end_seconds": 401.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.36,
      "text": "All the best."
    }
  ]
}